data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:18:50.810973+00:00", "content": "Based on my investigation of ce_branch24, I cannot push config changes - I'm a read-only network investigator. Let me share what I found:\n\n**Interface Status on ce_branch24:**\nAll interfaces (eth0, eth1, eth2, eth3, eth4, lo, vrf_CORP, vrf_VOICE, wg0) show **stable operational status = 1 (up)** across the entire investigation window with no flapping detected [metrics:0-99].\n\n**Traffic Analysis:**\n- **eth0** (primary): Steady traffic growth (~9.8M in / 3.7M out octets) [metrics:0-19, 9-17]\n- **eth1**: Low but stable traffic (~104K in / 79K out) [metrics:20-39, 10-12]\n- **eth2 & eth4**: Essentially idle (1746 octets constant) [metrics:40-59, 80-99, 11-13]\n- **eth3**: Steady low traffic (~102K in / 85K out) [metrics:60-79, 12-13]\n- **wg0** (WireGuard tunnel): Active tunnel traffic (~935K in / 956K out) [metrics:8, 17]\n\n**Error/Discard Check:**\n- Only **eth0** shows inbound discards (1877) [metrics:18]\n- All interfaces show **zero input/output errors** [metrics:27-35]\n- Output discards: eth0 has 4, others have 0 [from topology data]\n\n**Topology Context:**\nce_branch24 connects to pe12 (upstream PE) and has local VRFs for CORP and VOICE [topo:ce_branch24]. The upstream pe12 shows healthy BGP (2 peers established), OSPF, and MPLS [topo:pe12].\n\n**No evidence of interface flapping was found in the telemetry.** If you're seeing flapping from another source (syslog, SNMP traps, or a specific time window not captured here), please clarify:\n1. Which specific interface is flapping?\n2. What time window should I investigate?\n3. What symptoms are you observing (logs, alerts, user reports)?\n\nOnce identified, I can search for relevant runbooks and similar incidents to recommend the appropriate fix."}

